2. **Color Patterns and Markings**: Giraffes display a distinctive coat pattern consisting of irregular, brown patches separated by white lines. These patches vary in shape and size across different subspecies, but the overall pattern remains consistent within each individual. The coat serves as camouflage in their natural habitat, blending into the dappled light and shadow of the savanna.

